{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DSPgWhwsnur4YigniYgR82","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the discussion in the KIP-1163 design thread, I found the final decision on the metadata approach for diskless topics.\\\\n\\\\n## Final Decision\\\\n\\\\n**The decision was to build a new, independent metadata component for diskless topics rather than reusing the existing RLMM.**\\\\n\\\\nIn the May 12, 2026 discussion (`/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`), Jun Rao clearly stated:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis decision was endorsed by other participants. In the same discussion thread, Satish Duggana responded positively on May 13/14:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"RLMM was not designed for aggressive copying of the latest data to tiered storage by having small segment rollouts. +1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### Rationale\\\\n\\\\nThe decision was driven by the fact that RLMM has significant inefficiencies when used with the aggressive metadata generation patterns of diskless topics, including:\\\\n- Cost inefficiencies\\\\n- Metadata propagation delays\\\\n- Metadata storage overflow (potentially 100s of GB)\\\\n- Design mismatch with how diskless topics operate\\\\n\\\\nSource files:\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-01-mail-ab8f566d698775ad19a3d37d-2ac86e46.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":22.17,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":27299,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":60451,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1314629,\\\"input_tokens\\\":26,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1561}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e853c15-2c2b-46a9-87f5-2f44970152d7","uuid":"f9d35b27-b1c7-4dce-8cc1-3b6b5f3c0a1a","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:52:42.229Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the discussion in the KIP-1163 design thread, I found the final decision on the metadata approach for diskless topics.\\\\n\\\\n## Final Decision\\\\n\\\\n**The decision was to build a new, independent metadata component for diskless topics rather than reusing the existing RLMM.**\\\\n\\\\nIn the May 12, 2026 discussion (`/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`), Jun Rao clearly stated:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis decision was endorsed by other participants. In the same discussion thread, Satish Duggana responded positively on May 13/14:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"RLMM was not designed for aggressive copying of the latest data to tiered storage by having small segment rollouts. +1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### Rationale\\\\n\\\\nThe decision was driven by the fact that RLMM has significant inefficiencies when used with the aggressive metadata generation patterns of diskless topics, including:\\\\n- Cost inefficiencies\\\\n- Metadata propagation delays\\\\n- Metadata storage overflow (potentially 100s of GB)\\\\n- Design mismatch with how diskless topics operate\\\\n\\\\nSource files:\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-01-mail-ab8f566d698775ad19a3d37d-2ac86e46.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":22.17,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":27299,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":60451,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1314629,\\\"input_tokens\\\":26,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1561}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the discussion in the KIP-1163 design thread, I found the final decision on the metadata approach for diskless topics.\\n\\n## Final Decision\\n\\n**The decision was to build a new, independent metadata component for diskless topics rather than reusing the existing RLMM.**\\n\\nIn the May 12, 2026 discussion (`/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`), Jun Rao clearly stated:\\n\\n> \\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\"\\n\\nThis decision was endorsed by other participants. In the same discussion thread, Satish Duggana responded positively on May 13/14:\\n\\n> \\\"RLMM was not designed for aggressive copying of the latest data to tiered storage by having small segment rollouts. +1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\"\\n\\n### Rationale\\n\\nThe decision was driven by the fact that RLMM has significant inefficiencies when used with the aggressive metadata generation patterns of diskless topics, including:\\n- Cost inefficiencies\\n- Metadata propagation delays\\n- Metadata storage overflow (potentially 100s of GB)\\n- Design mismatch with how diskless topics operate\\n\\nSource files:\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md`\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md`\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-01-mail-ab8f566d698775ad19a3d37d-2ac86e46.md\",\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-12-mail-620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54-63a54ab3.md\",\"kips/KIP-1163/2026-05-14-mail-discuss-3e3a9a34.md\"],\"seconds\":22.17,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":27299,\"cache_write_tokens\":60451,\"cost_usd\":0.1314629,\"input_tokens\":26,\"output_tokens\":1561}}"}}}
